{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Data Management Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Install the datasets library"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pip install datasets huggingface_hub"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Load a dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from datasets import load_dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dataset = load_dataset(\"imdb\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(dataset)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(dataset[\"train\"][0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This downloads the IMDB movie review dataset. After the first download, it loads from cache at `~/.cache/huggingface/datasets/`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Stream large datasets"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Some datasets are too large to fit on disk. Streaming loads them row by row without downloading the full thing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dataset = load_dataset(\"wikimedia/wikipedia\", \"20220301.en\", split=\"train\", streaming=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for i, example in enumerate(dataset):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(example[\"title\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if i >= 4:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Streaming gives you an `IterableDataset`. You process rows as they arrive. Memory usage stays constant regardless of dataset size."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Dataset formats"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `datasets` library uses Apache Arrow under the hood. You can convert to other formats depending on what your pipeline needs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dataset = load_dataset(\"imdb\", split=\"train\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dataset.to_csv(\"imdb_train.csv\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dataset.to_json(\"imdb_train.json\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dataset.to_parquet(\"imdb_train.parquet\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Format comparison:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Format | Size | Read Speed | Best For |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|--------|------|-----------|----------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| CSV | Large | Slow | Human readability, spreadsheets |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| JSON | Large | Slow | APIs, nested data |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Parquet | Small | Fast | Analytics, columnar queries |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Arrow | Small | Fastest | In-memory processing (what `datasets` uses internally) |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For AI work, Parquet is the best storage format. Arrow is what you work with in memory. CSV and JSON are for interchange."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Data splits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every ML project needs three splits:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Train**: The model learns from this (typically 80%)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Validation**: You check progress during training (typically 10%)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Test**: Final evaluation after training is done (typically 10%)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Some datasets come pre-split. When they don't, split them yourself:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dataset = load_dataset(\"imdb\", split=\"train\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "split = dataset.train_test_split(test_size=0.2, seed=42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "train_val = split[\"train\"].train_test_split(test_size=0.125, seed=42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "train_ds = train_val[\"train\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "val_ds = train_val[\"test\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "test_ds = split[\"test\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Train: {len(train_ds)}, Val: {len(val_ds)}, Test: {len(test_ds)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Always set a seed for reproducibility. The same seed produces the same split every time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Download and cache models"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Models are large files. The `huggingface_hub` library handles downloading and caching."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from huggingface_hub import hf_hub_download, snapshot_download"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model_path = hf_hub_download("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    repo_id=\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    filename=\"config.json\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Cached at: {model_path}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model_dir = snapshot_download(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Full model at: {model_dir}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Models cache to `~/.cache/huggingface/hub/`. Once downloaded, they load instantly on subsequent runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Handle large files"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Model weights and large datasets should not go into git. Three options:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Option A: .gitignore (simplest)**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "*.bin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "*.safetensors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "*.pt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "*.onnx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "data/*.parquet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "data/*.csv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "models/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Option B: Git LFS (track large files in git)**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "git lfs install"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "git lfs track \"*.bin\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "git lfs track \"*.safetensors\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "git add .gitattributes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Git LFS stores pointers in your repo and the actual files on a separate server. GitHub gives you 1 GB free."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Option C: DVC (data version control)**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pip install dvc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dvc init"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dvc add data/training_set.parquet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "git add data/training_set.parquet.dvc data/.gitignore"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "git commit -m \"Track training data with DVC\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "DVC creates small `.dvc` files that point to your data. The data itself lives in S3, GCS, or another remote storage backend."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Approach | Complexity | Best For |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "|----------|-----------|----------|"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| .gitignore | Low | Personal projects, downloaded data you can re-fetch |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Git LFS | Medium | Teams sharing model weights via git |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| DVC | High | Reproducible experiments, large datasets, teams |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For this course, `.gitignore` is enough. Use DVC when you need to reproduce exact experiments across machines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 8: Storage patterns"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Local storage** works for datasets under ~10 GB. The HF cache handles this automatically."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Cloud storage** is for anything larger or shared across machines:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import os"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "local_path = os.path.expanduser(\"~/.cache/huggingface/datasets/\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# s3_path = \"s3://my-bucket/datasets/\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# gcs_path = \"gs://my-bucket/datasets/\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "DVC integrates with S3 and GCS directly:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dvc remote add -d myremote s3://my-bucket/dvc-store"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dvc push"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For this course, local storage is sufficient. Cloud storage becomes relevant when you fine-tune on remote GPU instances."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
